---
/**
 * ContentPanel override: a full-bleed canvas for the marketing surface.
 *
 * WHY THIS EXISTS
 *
 * The founder's brief (2026-11-07) is that a first-time visitor should feel
 * they are "entering a universe of AI education material", with the value
 * legible in the first three seconds. Our homepage could not do that, and the
 * reason was one declaration: stock ContentPanel caps its inner container at
 * `max-width: var(--sl-content-width)`, which is 45rem (720px). Everything
 * else about the page being sidebar-free was already true, because index.mdx
 * uses `template: splash`. So the "it looks like a wiki" feeling on the
 * homepage was a 720px prose column, not the framework.
 *
 * This override lifts that cap for the marketing routes only, which is what
 * lets a section own the full viewport width and carry its own background.
 * Astro and Starlight needed no replacing to get there.
 *
 * IMPORTANT, THE REASON THIS FILE COPIES STOCK CSS
 *
 * Overriding a Starlight component means the stock component never renders,
 * so ITS <style> block never ships either. The stock rules below are
 * reproduced verbatim from
 * node_modules/@astrojs/starlight/components/ContentPanel.astro so that the
 * 1,868 pages which are NOT marketing routes render byte-identically. On a
 * Starlight upgrade, re-diff against that file. If the stock rules change and
 * this copy does not, every lesson page silently loses the fix.
 *
 * SCOPE, deliberately narrow, and INERT UNTIL A PAGE ASKS
 *
 * Full bleed is opt-in from the page's own frontmatter (`full_bleed: true`)
 * and additionally requires `template: splash`. Two independent conditions,
 * because the cost of a false positive is high.
 *
 * ONE PAGE OPTS IN: src/content/docs/index.mdx, as of this commit, together
 * with the hero, catalog wall and stat band that give it edge-to-edge
 * sections to show.
 *
 * A correction worth keeping, because it changed what this commit had to do.
 * The earlier note here said that lifting the cap produced paragraphs 1425px
 * wide, about 166 characters per line. That measurement selected
 * `.sl-markdown-content > p`, DIRECT children only, and it returned exactly
 * one element. On this page that selector still returns exactly one element,
 * and it is <p class="lp-podcast-accent">: a centred flex row holding a label
 * and a badge, whose BOX is page-wide while its widest line box is 199px. So
 * the figure was an element box, not a line box, and the paragraph it seemed
 * to describe does not exist. Every actual paragraph here lives inside
 * .lp-section, which carries its own max-width: 54rem and margin-inline:
 * auto, so the cap on this panel was never what held them in.
 *
 * Re-measured properly with Range.getClientRects(), which returns one rect
 * per line box: the flip moves no prose line by a single pixel. Nineteen
 * blocks sat over 75 characters before the flip and the same nineteen sat
 * over it after, at identical widths. What the flip DID break was the page
 * footer, which is handled in its own rule below.
 *
 * The lesson stands even though the number was wrong: full bleed only helps a
 * page that SUPPLIES edge-to-edge sections, so the canvas shipped first and
 * unused, and the page joined it in the same commit as the sections that use
 * it.
 *
 * The flag lives on the page rather than in an allowlist here because that is
 * where the knowledge belongs: a page knows whether it has full-bleed
 * sections. It also makes joining a one-line change.
 *
 * Read-along safety: this changes layout only. It adds and removes no DOM text
 * node, so narration word indices cannot shift. It also never renders on a
 * lesson route.
 */
const { entry } = Astro.locals.starlightRoute;

/*
 * `full_bleed` is an optional boolean we add to the docs schema in
 * src/content.config.ts. Starlight types `starlightRoute.entry.data` from its
 * OWN base schema and does not thread user extensions through, so the field is
 * invisible to TypeScript here and a direct read fails `astro check`. The
 * narrow local type below is the documented shape of what we read, and nothing
 * more, so a typo in either field still fails the build.
 */
const data = entry.data as typeof entry.data & {
	template?: string;
	full_bleed?: boolean;
};

// The `template: splash` interlock means a lesson cannot opt in even by
// mistake, because lessons are never splash routes.
const isSplash = data.template === 'splash';
const fullBleed = isSplash && data.full_bleed === true;
---

<div class="content-panel" data-full-bleed={fullBleed ? 'true' : undefined}>
	<div class="sl-container"><slot /></div>
</div>

<style>
	@layer starlight.core {
		/* --- Stock Starlight rules, reproduced verbatim. Do not edit. --- */
		.content-panel {
			padding: 1.5rem var(--sl-content-pad-x);
		}
		.content-panel + .content-panel {
			border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline);
		}
		.sl-container {
			max-width: var(--sl-content-width);
		}

		.sl-container > :global(* + *) {
			margin-top: 1.5rem;
		}

		@media (min-width: 72rem) {
			.sl-container {
				margin-inline: var(--sl-content-margin-inline, auto);
			}
		}

		/* --- Clawdemy addition: the full-bleed marketing canvas. --- */

		/*
		 * Drop the panel's own gutter so a section can paint to both edges. A
		 * section that wants a readable text column re-establishes one itself,
		 * which is the right place for that decision: per section, not for the
		 * whole page.
		 */
		.content-panel[data-full-bleed] {
			padding: 0;
		}

		/* The cap itself, and the auto-centering that goes with it. */
		.content-panel[data-full-bleed] > .sl-container {
			max-width: none;
			margin-inline: 0;
		}

		/*
		 * Stock puts 1.5rem between adjacent children. Full-bleed bands set
		 * their own vertical rhythm, and an inherited margin between them
		 * would show as a stripe of page background between sections.
		 */
		.content-panel[data-full-bleed] > .sl-container > :global(* + *) {
			margin-top: 0;
		}

		/*
		 * Stock draws a hairline between stacked panels. On a designed landing
		 * page that reads as an accidental rule across the layout.
		 */
		.content-panel[data-full-bleed] + .content-panel,
		.content-panel + .content-panel[data-full-bleed] {
			border-top: 0;
		}

		/*
		 * THE FOOTER IS NOT A MARKETING SECTION.
		 *
		 * Starlight renders its page footer as a sibling of the content inside
		 * .sl-container, so dropping the panel gutter above drops the footer's
		 * gutter with it. Measured on the first flipped build: "Last updated:
		 * Nov 8, 2026" sat at x=1440 on a 1440px viewport, hard against the
		 * glass, because the meta row is right-aligned.
		 *
		 * The sections on this page each own their width. The footer does not
		 * and should not, so the canvas hands it back the same wrap and gutter
		 * the hero and the stat band use, which also lines all three up on one
		 * pair of vertical rules.
		 *
		 * :global() is required: the footer is Starlight's element, not this
		 * component's, so Astro would otherwise scope the selector to markup
		 * that never matches.
		 */
		.content-panel[data-full-bleed] > .sl-container > :global(footer) {
			max-width: var(--v2-wrap);
			margin-inline: auto;
			padding-inline: var(--fl-gutter);
		}
	}
</style>
